* Hermetic ngspice init for sim/inductor-model.
*
* run_model_check.sh copies this file into the scratch directory it runs
* ngspice from, so a run does NOT depend on whether $HOME/.spiceinit exists
* (the PDK ships libs.tech/ngspice/install.py, which symlinks one into $HOME;
* a cold-start checkout on a machine where that was never run must still
* reproduce the committed numbers).
*
* ngbehavior=hsa is the compatibility mode the PDK's own .spiceinit sets, and
* is what its model libraries are written against. sg13g2_inductor_analytic.spice
* uses only ngspice-native R/L/C primitives and .param arithmetic, so the mode
* is not load-bearing here; it is set anyway so this tree matches the PDK's
* documented ngspice setup rather than quietly diverging from it, and so the
* model behaves identically when it is .include'd alongside the PDK libraries
* by sim/tank-characterization/run_pvt_sweep.sh.
set ngbehavior=hsa
